<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cape Coast</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cape Coast is a port town on the coast of present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghana">Ghana</a>, in the lands of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> kingdom of Fetu. The Swedish <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> Company built <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-coast-castle">Fort Carolusborg</a> there in 1653, which passed through Danish and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> hands before the English took it in 1664 and made Cape Coast Castle their headquarters on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-coast">Gold Coast</a>. It was a major point of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a> and the seat of British administration until 1877.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cape-coast.jpg" alt="Cape Coast" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Own work · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cape_Coast_Montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
